# Docs
docs/

# Dev tooling — not part of the shipped module archive.
node_modules/

# Release build output — `npm run package` and CI write the archive here.
dist/

# Test / tooling output
coverage/
.vitest/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# End-to-end harness. The *source* is tracked: it drives a real Foundry install against real
# content modules and is where the module's trade authority is actually verified. It is never
# shipped, so being tracked and being released are separate questions. Two things stay out:
#
#   config.mjs  absolute paths to one machine's Foundry install and user data
#   run output  the logs and reports quote item text from content packs
test-e2e/config.mjs
test-e2e/*.log
test-e2e/*.jsonl
test-e2e/*.html
# Dropped by shell.mjs and screenshots.mjs when a run fails — a picture of the broken world.
test-e2e/failure.png
